    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "35"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 345.839, 53.341, 484.219, 286.742 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "It is incumbent upon us to coordinate the management of this condition with the patient’s gynecologist or personal physician. Chlamydia is one of the leading causes of female infertility. Our patients—and their sexual partners—need medical care and counseling for the non-ocular aspects of this sexually transmitted disease. Chlamydia should also be reported to the local health department, which can be done online on a state-bystate basis."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.839, 53.341, 172.199, 231.142 ],
    "font" : "Palatino-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "In reviewing the signs and symptoms, this patient may seem to have both a viral and a bacterial infection at the same time. A key point in the differential diagnosis is the asymmetry of the follicles between the two eyes. With fluorescein staining, one eye may have giant inferior follicles, while the other eye has a limited follicular response, if"
  }, {
